    "generator": "NumPy PCG64; signed fixed coefficients and seeded scaling; overlapping and missing source labels",
    "cache_policy": "Clear all three scalar arithmetic caches before each method; fresh solver per method/trial; alternate method order by dataset index + trial",
    "workload": "Both methods share one GraphEngine load and cohort. Each solves all four budget cells for the same three compounds. Naive shares each full-world rerank across all three; envelopes share all slices across all three.",
    "timing": "perf_counter wall seconds; setup, solve, shared load/cohort and independent verification are separate; ratios exclude verification and shared load/cohort",
    "independence": "Naive independently recomputes full sparse path products and ranks in each world, without contribution tables, envelopes, production rank helpers or production replay; the finite arithmetic scorer is deliberately shared",
    "verification": "All four frontier cells and action counts match exhaustive results; every certificate verifies; every emitted witness is independently recomputed by full sparse products",
    "limitations": "Small synthetic graphs on one recorded runtime, fixed degrees and one disease; no claim about Hetionet-scale latency, asymptotic exponent, predictive accuracy or general graph neural networks; runtime ratios include Python and certificate serialization overhead. The reference is literal exhaustive recomputation, not the fastest possible exhaustive solver."
